# mgleak.msg - text of the three leaking pipes (mgleak.ssl). One entry per line; no braces in comments.

# 100 to 105: look (pipe leaking, pipe patched, steam) and examine in the same order.
{100}{}{You see a leaking water pipe.}
{101}{}{You see a patched water pipe.}
{102}{}{You see a jet of water and steam.}
{103}{}{The pipe has split along a seam somebody welded before the War and somebody else re-welded after it. It is losing water faster than a desert town can afford. It wants a repairman, or at least a lump of scrap hammered into it.}
{104}{}{The split is closed. The patch is ugly, which puts it in keeping with the rest of the town.}
{105}{}{Water under pressure, leaving. It is warm, it smells of rust, and it will go on going to waste until somebody repairs the pipe behind it.}

# 110 to 113: the pipe, heard from close by.
{110}{}{Hsssssss.}
{111}{}{Drip. Drip. Hsss.}
{112}{}{Ssssss-pt. Ssssss.}
{113}{}{Fsssssh.}

# 120 to 124: an attempt to fix it.
{120}{}{It has stopped leaking. Hitting it again would not improve it.}
{121}{}{You work the seam shut and tighten the collar until the hiss dies. The pipe holds.}
{122}{}{You hammer a lump of scrap into the split and bend it over. It is not pretty. The pipe holds.}
{123}{}{You can see what is wrong: the seam has opened and wants plugging. With a piece of junk metal to hammer into it, you could close it.}
{124}{}{You make it worse for a moment, then it settles back to a steady drip. This needs someone who knows pipes, or at least knows a little and has a tool or two.}

# 130 to 132: after a leak is closed.
{130}{}{Somewhere else in town, another pipe is still hissing.}
{131}{}{That was the last of the three. Walter at the water plant will want to hear about it.}
{132}{}{That was the last of the three. With Walter dead, nobody is left to pay you for it. The town will drink all the same.}

{140}{}{Science confirms it: this is a pipe, and the water is on the wrong side of it.}
{141}{}{It is a pipe. It does not need you.}
